eta.Grind.Solvers.newEq","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Types.lean#L2717-L2719"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Solvers.propagateDiseqs\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Grind</span>.<span class=\"name\">Solvers</span>.<span class=\"name\">propagateDiseqs</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">lhs </span><span class=\"fn\">rhs</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.GoalM\">GoalM</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit\">Unit</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Given a new disequality `lhs ≠ rhs`, propagates it to relevant theories.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Solvers.propagateDiseqs","kind":"def","line":2613,"name":"Lean.Meta.Grind.Solvers.propagateDiseqs","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Types.lean#L2613-L2650"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Solvers.mkActionCore\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Grind</span>.<span class=\"name\">Solvers</span>.<span class=\"name\">mkActionCore</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/System/IO.html#IO\">IO</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Action\">Action</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Combines the active solver extensions into a single action using `Action.andAlso`.\nDoes not drain `newRawFacts`; use `Solvers.mkAction` (defined in `Intro.lean`) which\nwraps this with `assertAll`.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Solvers.mkActionCore","kind":"def","line":2579,"name":"Lean.Meta.Grind.Solvers.mkActionCore","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Types.lean#L2579-L2589"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Action.andAlso\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Grind</span>.<span class=\"name\">Action</span>.<span class=\"name\">andAlso</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x </span><span class=\"fn\">y</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Action\">Action</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Action\">Action</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Sequential conjunction: executes both `x` and `y`.\n\n- Runs `x` and always runs `y` afterward, regardless of whether `x` made progress.\n- It is not applicable only if both `x` and `y` are not applicable.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Action.andAlso","kind":"def","line":2570,"name":"Lean.Meta.Grind.Action.andAlso","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Types.lean#L2570-L2577"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Solvers.mbtc\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</s