html#Lean.Meta.Grind.PreInstance.mk","kind":"ctor","line":985,"name":"Lean.Meta.Grind.PreInstance.mk","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Types.lean#L985-L1005"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">structure</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.PreInstance\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Grind</span>.<span class=\"name\">PreInstance</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The E-matching module instantiates theorems using the `EMatchTheorem proof` and a (partial) assignment.\nWe want to avoid instantiating the same theorem with the same assignment more than once.\nTherefore, we store the (pre-)instance information in set.\nRecall that the proofs of activated theorems have been hash-consed.\nThe assignment contains internalized expressions, which have also been hash-consed.\n\n**Note**: We used to use pointer equality to implement `PreInstanceSet`. However,\nthis low-level trick was incorrect in interactive mode because we add new\n`EMatchTheorem` objects using `instantiate [...]`. For example, suppose we write\n```\ninstantiate [thm_1]; instantiate [thm_1]\n```\nThe `EMatchTheorem` object `thm_1` is created twice. Using pointer equality will\nmiss instances created using the two different objects. Recall we do not use\nhash-consing on proof objects. If we hash-cons the proof objects, it would be ok\nto use pointer equality.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.PreInstance","kind":"structure","line":985,"name":"Lean.Meta.Grind.PreInstance","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Types.lean#L985-L1005"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">abbrev</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.ParentMap\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Grind</span>.<span class=\"name\">ParentMap</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.ParentMap","kind":"def","line":983,"name":"Lean.Meta.Grind.ParentMap","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Types.lean#L983-L983"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.ParentSet.elems\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Grind</span>.<span class=\"name\">ParentSet</span>.<span class=\"name\">elems</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">ps</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.ParentSet\">ParentSet</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#List\">List</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.ParentSet.elems","kind":"def","line":980,"name":"Lean.Meta.Grind.ParentSet.elems","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Types.lean#L980-L981"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/T